IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`

-- Regulation 2 (interpretation), the definitions about bodies and enactments: local authority, local welfare provision, enactment.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- local authority. The list depends on the nation: England, Wales and Scotland name different kinds of council.
-- src:62 | “local authority” means—
-- src:63 | (a) in relation to England, a county council, a district council, a parish council, a London borough council, the Common Council of the City of London or the Council of the Isles of Scilly;
-- src:64 | (b) in relation to Wales, a county council, a county borough council or a community council;
-- src:65 | (c) in relation to Scotland, a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994 ;
@ref reg 2 "local authority" (src:62-65)
DECLARE `Kind of council` IS ONE OF
    `a county council`
    `a district council`
    `a parish council`
    `a London borough council`
    `the Common Council of the City of London`
    `the Council of the Isles of Scilly`
    `a county borough council`
    `a community council`
    `a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994`
    `another kind of body`

DECLARE `Body that may be a local authority` HAS
    `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked`  IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
    `kind of body`                                              IS A `Kind of council`

-- src:62 | “local authority” means—
-- src:63 | (a) in relation to England, a county council, a district council, a parish council, a London borough council, the Common Council of the City of London or the Council of the Isles of Scilly;
-- src:64 | (b) in relation to Wales, a county council, a county borough council or a community council;
-- src:65 | (c) in relation to Scotland, a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994 ;
@ref reg 2 "local authority" (src:62-65)
GIVEN body IS A `Body that may be a local authority`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — local authority` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body's `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked`
    WHEN England THEN
        CONSIDER body's `kind of body`
        WHEN `a county council`                           THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a district council`                         THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a parish council`                           THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a London borough council`                   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the Common Council of the City of London`   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the Council of the Isles of Scilly`         THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN Wales THEN
        CONSIDER body's `kind of body`
        WHEN `a county council`                           THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a county borough council`                   THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a community council`                        THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN Scotland THEN
        CONSIDER body's `kind of body`
        WHEN `a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- local welfare provision: occasional financial or other assistance, given by a local authority, the Scottish Ministers,
-- the Welsh Ministers or a person authorised to act for or provide a service to them, to or for individuals, for either of
-- two purposes. Whether the giver is a local authority is `reg 2 — local authority`; the choice is made by the caller.
-- src:66 | “local welfare provision” means occasional financial or other assistance given by a local authority, the Scottish Ministers or the Welsh Ministers, or a person authorised to exercise any function of, or provide a service to, them, to or in respect of individuals for the purpose of—
@ref reg 2 "local welfare provision" (src:66)
DECLARE `Giver of assistance` IS ONE OF
    `a local authority`
    `the Scottish Ministers`
    `the Welsh Ministers`
    `a person authorised to exercise any function of, or provide a service to, a local authority or the Scottish Ministers or the Welsh Ministers`
    `another giver`

-- src:66 | “local welfare provision” means occasional financial or other assistance given by a local authority, the Scottish Ministers or the Welsh Ministers, or a person authorised to exercise any function of, or provide a service to, them, to or in respect of individuals for the purpose of—
-- src:67 | (a) meeting, or helping to meet, an immediate short term need—
-- src:68 | (i) arising out of an exceptional event, or exceptional circumstances; and
-- src:69 | (ii) that requires to be met in order to avoid a risk to the well-being of an individual; or
-- src:70 | (b) enabling individuals to establish or maintain a settled home, where those individuals have been or, without the assistance, might otherwise be—
-- src:71 | (i) in prison, hospital, a residential care establishment or other institution; or
-- src:72 | (ii) homeless or otherwise living an unsettled way of life;
@ref reg 2 "local welfare provision" (src:66-72)
DECLARE `Assistance given to individuals` HAS
    giver                                                                                   IS A `Giver of assistance`
    `assistance is occasional financial or other assistance`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose is meeting, or helping to meet, an immediate short term need`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `need arises out of an exceptional event, or exceptional circumstances`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `need requires to be met in order to avoid a risk to the well-being of an individual`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose is enabling individuals to establish or maintain a settled home`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `individuals have been or, without the assistance, might otherwise be in prison, hospital, a residential care establishment or other institution`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `individuals have been or, without the assistance, might otherwise be homeless or otherwise living an unsettled way of life`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:66 | “local welfare provision” means occasional financial or other assistance given by a local authority, the Scottish Ministers or the Welsh Ministers, or a person authorised to exercise any function of, or provide a service to, them, to or in respect of individuals for the purpose of—
@ref reg 2 "local welfare provision" (src:66)
GIVEN assistance IS AN `Assistance given to individuals`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — local welfare provision, the giver` assistance MEANS
    CONSIDER assistance's giver
    WHEN `a local authority`                                                                                                                              THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Scottish Ministers`                                                                                                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Welsh Ministers`                                                                                                                            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person authorised to exercise any function of, or provide a service to, a local authority or the Scottish Ministers or the Welsh Ministers` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another giver`                                                                                                                                  THEN FALSE

-- src:67 | (a) meeting, or helping to meet, an immediate short term need—
-- src:68 | (i) arising out of an exceptional event, or exceptional circumstances; and
-- src:69 | (ii) that requires to be met in order to avoid a risk to the well-being of an individual; or
@ref reg 2 "local welfare provision" limb (a) (src:67-69)
GIVEN assistance IS AN `Assistance given to individuals`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — local welfare provision, limb (a)` assistance MEANS
    (assistance's `purpose is meeting, or helping to meet, an immediate short term need`)
    AND (assistance's `need arises out of an exceptional event, or exceptional circumstances`)
    AND (assistance's `need requires to be met in order to avoid a risk to the well-being of an individual`)

-- src:70 | (b) enabling individuals to establish or maintain a settled home, where those individuals have been or, without the assistance, might otherwise be—
-- src:71 | (i) in prison, hospital, a residential care establishment or other institution; or
-- src:72 | (ii) homeless or otherwise living an unsettled way of life;
@ref reg 2 "local welfare provision" limb (b) (src:70-72)
GIVEN assistance IS AN `Assistance given to individuals`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — local welfare provision, limb (b)` assistance MEANS
    (assistance's `purpose is enabling individuals to establish or maintain a settled home`)
    AND (    (assistance's `individuals have been or, without the assistance, might otherwise be in prison, hospital, a residential care establishment or other institution`)
          OR (assistance's `individuals have been or, without the assistance, might otherwise be homeless or otherwise living an unsettled way of life`))

-- src:66 | “local welfare provision” means occasional financial or other assistance given by a local authority, the Scottish Ministers or the Welsh Ministers, or a person authorised to exercise any function of, or provide a service to, them, to or in respect of individuals for the purpose of—
-- src:67 | (a) meeting, or helping to meet, an immediate short term need—
-- src:68 | (i) arising out of an exceptional event, or exceptional circumstances; and
-- src:69 | (ii) that requires to be met in order to avoid a risk to the well-being of an individual; or
-- src:70 | (b) enabling individuals to establish or maintain a settled home, where those individuals have been or, without the assistance, might otherwise be—
-- src:71 | (i) in prison, hospital, a residential care establishment or other institution; or
-- src:72 | (ii) homeless or otherwise living an unsettled way of life;
@ref reg 2 "local welfare provision" (src:66-72)
GIVEN assistance IS AN `Assistance given to individuals`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 2 — local welfare provision` assistance MEANS
    (`reg 2 — local welfare provision, the giver` assistance)
    AND (assistance's `assistance is occasional financial or other assistance`)
    AND ((`reg 2 — local welfare provision, limb (a)` assistance) OR (`reg 2 — local welfare provision, limb (b)` assistance))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- enactment: the definition says "includes", so it adds two things and does not say what an enactment is. It can answer yes
-- for those two things and cannot answer no for anything. The explicit outcome `not decided by the definition of enactment`
-- stands for everything else (fork F5 in NOTES.md).
-- src:45 | “enactment” includes an enactment comprised in, or an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales;
@ref reg 2 "enactment" (src:45)
DECLARE `Whether the definition of enactment applies` IS ONE OF
    `included by the definition of enactment`
    `not decided by the definition of enactment`

DECLARE `Provision whose standing as an enactment is asked` HAS
    `enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales`    IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:45 | “enactment” includes an enactment comprised in, or an instrument made under, an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales;
@ref reg 2 "enactment" (src:45)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision whose standing as an enactment is asked`
GIVETH A `Whether the definition of enactment applies`
`reg 2 — enactment` provision MEANS
    IF (provision's `enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales`) OR (provision's `instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament or the National Assembly of Wales`)
    THEN `included by the definition of enactment`
    ELSE `not decided by the definition of enactment`
